# Apex 26 — Cursor entry

- **Rules:** read root `AGENTS.md` (canonical). Root `CLAUDE.md` is a stub that
  imports it; do not edit rules into `CLAUDE.md`.
- **Skills:** `.claude/skills/*/SKILL.md` (shared with Claude Code). Do not add
  a parallel `.cursor/skills/` tree unless a skill is Cursor-only.
- **Subagents:** `.claude/agents/*.md` (e.g. `deploy-research` for tinyfish
  post-deploy / public-web research). Prefer these over inventing ad-hoc
  workers for the same job.
- **MCP:** `.mcp.json` → `probe` / `tinyfish` / `chrome-devtools`. Live game or
  deploy checks: skill `mcp-probe` (thin index — traps/recipes load on demand
  under `references/`). Never run Chrome MCP while Playwright is running;
  never hand a subagent a browser test group. Prefer subagent `deploy-research`
  for tinyfish noise; do not attach fat skills unless the task needs them.
- **Token hygiene:** one skill per task; prefer `__apex` / `verify-track` /
  `test:tooling-fast` before screenshots or browser groups. Path-scoped rules
  under `.cursor/rules/` (e.g. `render-wgx`, `render-tlx`) attach by globs.
